  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">REACH3: Response to the Unmet Humanitarian Needs of vulnerable IDPs  in Mindanao</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is designed to provide the minimum basic needs through direct food assistance, construction and repair of Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH) facilities and provision of supplies and information campaign for improved hygiene practices, primary health care services including psycho -social support, provision of shelter and support to camp management and protection services implemented as a stand alone result area and as a mainstreamed principle across all the components of the assistance. A rapid response mechanism will also be put in place and enhanced in collaboration with the Local Government Units (LGUs) in selected areas, both as protocols applied in response to new disasters and to build local capacities for timely and appropriate emergency action in future disaster events.</narrative>
  </description>
